    },
    {
      "id": "t_1760",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 90,
      "y": 975.0,
      "width": 940,
      "height": 180.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "text": "the write guard  \u2014  why concurrent recomputes are safe\n\ncompute() runs OUTSIDE the mutex (it is the slow part: two DB reads).\nThe write is guarded on the valid-solve ROW COUNT \u2014 a data-derived version,\nnot wall time: the log is append-only, so more rows is strictly newer.\nA slow older recompute that finishes late is DROPPED, never a clobber.\n\nA timestamp would NOT be safe: the gap between reading the clock and\nPostgres taking its snapshot lets a later-stamped recompute read fewer rows.\n\nRecomputeForce (admin hide/delete, which legitimately SHRINKS the board)\n= one unconditional write + an immediately following guarded re-run.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "r_1758",
      "originalText": "the write guard  \u2014  why concurrent recomputes are safe\n\ncompute() runs OUTSIDE the mutex (it is the slow part: two DB reads).\nThe write is guarded on the valid-solve ROW COUNT \u2014 a data-derived version,\nnot wall time: the log is append-only, so more rows is strictly newer.\nA slow older recompute that finishes late is DROPPED, never a clobber.\n\nA timestamp would NOT be safe: the gap between reading the clock and\nPostgres taking its snapshot lets a later-stamped recompute read fewer rows.\n\nRecomputeForce (admin hide/delete, which legitimately SHRINKS the board)\n= one unconditional write + an immediately following guarded re-run.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
